    section=f'''<section class="card" id="motor-options"><div class="section-head"><h2>POC motor alternatives</h2><a href="motor-options-rfq.txt" download>Stock enquiry brief ↓</a></div><p class="compact-context">Checked 24 Oct 2026 · Dubai / Ankara / San Francisco · calculations only; saved CFD is unchanged</p><p><strong>First choice to seek: Gast 2AM-NCC-16 for a contained bench POC.</strong> Try the ~200 W lower-duty point if its load fixture is easier to obtain. It uses less air than the original motor. It is not predicted to beat LZB46's motor temperature drop. No alternative's immediate delivery is confirmed.</p><div class="table"><table><thead><tr><th>Motor / operating point</th><th>Shaft W</th><th>g/s</th><th>Motor ΔT K</th><th>Nozzle °C<br>old UA / short UA</th><th>Tank spray s</th><th>US list USD</th></tr></thead><tbody>{table}</tbody></table></div><p class="note">22°C assumed <strong>at the motor inlet</strong>, 30°C ambient. Gast values are approximate paired curve reads: interpolate 7/5.6 bar to 6.3 bar at the same speed; low-duty 2AM uses 5.6 bar / 1000 rpm. Free-air density assumed 1.2 kg/m³. Nozzle columns use UA=10.0737 / 1 W/K; neither conductance is a motor guarantee. Tank: 12 L / 200 bar / 22°C to 20 bar; adiabatic/isothermal inventory-only scenarios. No startup conditioning budget deducted.</p><details class="compact-details"><summary>Availability / procurement routes</summary><p>UAE and Turkey supply routes exist. Immediate stock remains unresolved; neither market is ruled out.</p><ul>{channels_html}</ul><p class="note">Zoro product descriptions such as “Stock 40/Skid” are not live inventory. Prices and catalogue pages do not establish ready-to-ship stock. 4AM-NRV-50CLL is marked discontinued in Zoro's listing; no matched oil-free curve/stock is qualified. 2AM-NCC-96 has conflicting retailer power fields and is excluded.</p></details><details class="compact-details"><summary>How to show cooling legitimately</summary><ol>{''.join('<li>'+esc(x)+'</li>' for x in poc)}</ol><p class="note">The standard Gast models above need lubrication. LL/NLP models have different pressure limits (manual: 5.5 bar), so they require separate curves and calculations. New cold-air temperatures are first-law scenarios; no new spatial CFD or 20–50 cm result is claimed.</p></details><details class="compact-details"><summary>Equations / curves / uncertainty</summary><div class="formula-equation">ṁ = ρfree Qfree<br>ΔTmotor = (Wshaft − Qinto_motor)/(ṁ cp)<br>Tnozzle = Ta + (Tin − ΔTmotor − Ta) exp[−UA/(ṁ cp)]<br>t = V(ρfill−ρcutoff)/ṁ</div><p class="note">Heat into the motor is zero in the nominal calculation. JSON includes a 25% shaft-heat-return scenario and ±10% power/flow sensitivity. These are assumptions, not error bounds. At startup, motor/fixture thermal storage must be included.</p><div class="links">{sources_html}<a href="motor-options.json">Full calculation / source record</a><a href="motor-options.csv">CSV</a><a href="motor-options-validation.json">30 numerical checks</a></div></details></section>'''
